##  Dashboards

### 1. HR Attrition Overview Dashboard
Provides an overall view of employee attrition and workforce statistics. It highlights key metrics such as total employees, attrition count, and attrition rate, along with an overview of employee distribution.

### 2. Employee Demographics Dashboard
Analyzes employee demographics such as age, gender, marital status, and education. It helps understand how employee characteristics are distributed and how they relate to attrition.

### 3. Job & Department Analysis Dashboard
Examines attrition across different departments, job roles, job levels, and overtime categories. It helps identify areas where employee turnover is relatively higher.

### 4. Income & Experience Dashboard
Analyzes employee income and work experience in relation to attrition. It includes factors such as monthly income, years at the company, total working years, and years in the current role.

### 5. Employee Satisfaction & Attrition Dashboard
Explores the relationship between employee satisfaction and attrition using factors such as job satisfaction, work-life balance, and other workplace-related attributes.
